{
  "slug": "artist:oscar-mulero",
  "name": "Oscar Mulero",
  "editorial_article": "Oscar Mulero, born Óscar Mulero Crecente, began his career in Madrid clubs like New World and Overdrive during the late 1980s, eventually founding his influential Omen Club in 1994. Since the turn of the millennium, he has managed two primary imprints, Warm Up Recordings and PoleGroup Recordings, both of which contain more than 100 releases in their respective catalogs. His discography spans various projects and aliases, including Trolley Route, Dr Smoke, and Infamous Monster, while his 2012 studio album Black Propaganda earned recognition within the underground community for its uncompromising approach. Beyond his solo work, he has collaborated with artists such as Ben Sims, Exium, Christian Wünsch, and Umwelt. His output consistently bridges styles ranging from abrasive, hard-hitting techno to ambient and experimental compositions, marking his evolution since his early EBM-influenced DJ sets in Spain.",
